WEBVTT

00:00.553 --> 00:03.615
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.682 --> 00:07.043
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.095 --> 00:10.189
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.257 --> 00:13.168
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.235 --> 00:17.116
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.167 --> 00:20.062
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.130 --> 00:21.652
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:21.720 --> 00:23.023
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.108 --> 00:26.203
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.623 --> 00:35.893
(doorbell ringing)

00:37.633 --> 00:39.006
Oh, hi, Bonnie.
What's up?

00:39.097 --> 00:41.722
Hi, Lois, um,
I hate to bother you,

00:41.790 --> 00:44.199
but I'm going out
of town for a few days

00:44.267 --> 00:45.922
to visit my father
in the hospital.

00:45.989 --> 00:47.795
I was hoping that
while I was gone,

00:47.863 --> 00:49.754
you could look in
on Susie and Joe.

00:49.822 --> 00:51.393
And go have sex
with Quagmire.

00:51.462 --> 00:52.631
Quagmire!
Quagmire!

00:52.699 --> 00:54.573
Aw, shucks, you can't
blame a guy for trying.

00:54.642 --> 00:56.681
Giggity-giggity-giggity!

00:56.749 --> 00:58.939
(squeaking)

00:59.007 --> 01:01.701
Well, of course, Bonnie.
I'd love to help.

01:01.769 --> 01:03.156
Meg, sweetie?

01:03.224 --> 01:04.378
Yeah, Mom?

01:04.447 --> 01:06.336
Bonnie wants you to look
after Susie and Joe

01:06.421 --> 01:08.175
while she's out of town.

01:08.244 --> 01:09.851
What?! Why me?!

01:09.918 --> 01:11.573
I don't want to
have to do that.

01:11.641 --> 01:13.815
And Bonnie said
you are very pretty.

01:13.882 --> 01:15.890
But I... How did
that come up?

01:15.958 --> 01:17.162
Oh, y-you know...

01:17.230 --> 01:18.901
we were talking
about pretty people.

01:18.969 --> 01:20.642
And-- and I said
Rachel Maddow,

01:20.710 --> 01:23.821
and she kind of took the baton
from there and said Meg Griffin.

01:23.889 --> 01:25.362
Who's Rachel Maddow?

01:25.430 --> 01:27.503
A model.

01:27.571 --> 01:28.673
Oh.

01:28.741 --> 01:30.648
Yeah.

01:30.717 --> 01:32.389
Okay, I'll do it.

01:36.841 --> 01:37.777
(laughing)

01:37.845 --> 01:39.299
Whoops.

01:39.367 --> 01:41.290
Oh, hey, uh,
excuse me, fella?

01:41.342 --> 01:43.348
Yeah, what do
you want, shrimp?

01:43.433 --> 01:45.140
Oh, just a few moments
of your time.

01:45.208 --> 01:46.310
Hang on.

01:46.362 --> 01:48.117
Let me just get
this little guy assembled.

01:48.186 --> 01:50.661
♪ Doo, doo, doo, doo, doo,
doo, doo, doodie, doo. ♪

01:50.730 --> 01:51.950
So where you from?

01:52.018 --> 01:53.874
Newburyport.
What's it to you?

01:53.941 --> 01:56.618
Oh, I'm just always interested
in where people are from.

01:56.685 --> 01:58.759
Everybody's got a story,
that's what I believe.

01:58.827 --> 02:00.366
All right, I think
we're all set here.

02:02.509 --> 02:03.913
(laughing)

02:05.404 --> 02:08.749
Wow. Never seen
that happen before.

02:08.817 --> 02:10.054
What the devil
happened here?

02:10.122 --> 02:11.560
I've assembled that
rifle a million times.

02:11.629 --> 02:13.535
Well, I don't know
if it's just the rifle.

02:13.603 --> 02:14.639
What are you talking about?

02:14.706 --> 02:16.163
I think you're going soft.

02:16.229 --> 02:18.404
I mean, when was the last time
you tried to blow something up,

02:18.472 --> 02:19.692
or take over the world,

02:19.760 --> 02:21.233
or even used the phrase,
"Damn you"?

02:21.300 --> 02:23.240
Hey, I got a lot
on my plate, man.

02:23.308 --> 02:25.952
I'm learning to use the toilet,
I'm learning what shapes are.

02:26.019 --> 02:28.494
I-I spent half an hour laughing
at my own feet yesterday.

02:28.562 --> 02:30.804
Yeah, you're losing it, man.
You're losing your edge.

02:30.871 --> 02:32.443
Well, I don't care
for your tone

02:32.511 --> 02:35.588
and I'd say you deserve a good
kick in the... (laughing)

02:35.656 --> 02:36.693
Oh, look!

02:36.761 --> 02:38.132
Oh, Brian, look at them!

02:43.103 --> 02:45.327
JOE:
Come in.

02:45.395 --> 02:48.775
Drop it, creep-o!

02:48.842 --> 02:51.218
Don't move,
Catherine Deneuve!

02:51.286 --> 02:54.096
Freezerino, Paul Sorvino!

02:54.180 --> 02:55.818
What are you doing,
Mr. Swanson?

02:55.886 --> 02:58.078
I'm tryin' out
some cop entrances.

02:58.145 --> 03:02.110
Oh, well, I'm here to help
you out while Bonnie's gone.

03:02.178 --> 03:03.784
Oh, great.

03:03.851 --> 03:05.121
Uh, do you have
any experience

03:05.190 --> 03:06.797
helping out people
with special needs?

03:06.864 --> 03:09.539
Well, I did work for that
old lady down the street.

03:09.607 --> 03:13.422
Meg, could you come
here, please?

03:13.490 --> 03:14.827
What is it?

03:14.894 --> 03:17.672
Could you see if I'm getting
a bed sore on my back?

03:17.739 --> 03:19.980
Sure.

03:20.049 --> 03:21.486
It looks fine
to me, ma'am.

03:21.554 --> 03:23.126
Thank you, dear.

03:23.194 --> 03:25.285
I must have just
slept on it wrong.

03:25.352 --> 03:26.322
(laughing)

03:26.391 --> 03:27.695
I stole Meg's cutaway.

03:33.903 --> 03:36.044
(whooshing) What the hell
is going on in here?

03:36.112 --> 03:37.818
Well, Brian, I thought
about what you said

03:37.886 --> 03:39.458
at the park, and I've
decided you're right.

03:39.526 --> 03:40.729
I have gone soft.

03:40.797 --> 03:42.855
I've lost my
sadistic streak.

03:42.923 --> 03:45.247
So I've built a concentrated
neural enhancement device,

03:45.315 --> 03:46.837
designed to boost
my evil side.

03:46.904 --> 03:49.397
All right, shall we take
this thing for a spin?

03:49.465 --> 03:51.455
Now, when I say so,
hit that button.

03:54.803 --> 03:56.156
Okay, hit it.

03:56.225 --> 03:57.530
(electronic whirring)

03:57.597 --> 04:00.272
(whirring grows louder)

04:00.341 --> 04:01.678
(whooshing)

04:11.217 --> 04:13.141
Well, how do you feel?

04:13.209 --> 04:14.329
I don't know.

04:14.397 --> 04:15.968
I don't feel any different.

04:16.036 --> 04:17.794
Well, why don't you
try insulting me?

04:17.862 --> 04:18.897
Yeah, okay.

04:18.965 --> 04:21.775
Um, sometimes you
chase helicopters.

04:21.843 --> 04:23.080
That's kind of lame.

04:23.149 --> 04:24.570
Yeah. Um...

04:24.637 --> 04:26.644
Besides, I do that
to protect the house.

04:26.712 --> 04:29.456
Helicopters are going to hurt
us, and I make them stay away.

04:29.524 --> 04:31.329
You know what?
Didn't look at it that way.

04:31.397 --> 04:33.037
Thank you for protecting us.

04:33.104 --> 04:34.510
Look, your machine
obviously didn't work.

04:34.577 --> 04:36.182
It just needs a few
adjustments, that's all.

04:36.250 --> 04:38.458
Come on, help me get
some of Peter's tools out

04:38.509 --> 04:39.880
of the "gay-rage."

04:45.303 --> 04:47.879
(electronic whirring)

04:49.352 --> 04:52.011
(beeping)

05:00.680 --> 05:02.519
♪ ♪

05:08.277 --> 05:12.978
...97, 98, 99, 100.

05:13.062 --> 05:14.952
Ah, thanks, Meg.

05:15.020 --> 05:18.382
I really appreciate you helping
me out these past couple of days.

05:18.450 --> 05:19.788
Sorry I bit you yesterday.

05:19.856 --> 05:21.260
That's okay.

05:21.328 --> 05:24.038
I guess now I know not to get
too close to your bowl, right?

05:24.106 --> 05:25.812
(chuckles)
Yeah.

05:25.880 --> 05:28.824
I know you're not trying to hurt
me, but part of me doesn't know.

05:31.836 --> 05:33.844
Oh my God, is it ten of 8:00?

05:33.911 --> 05:35.500
Aw, damn it, I missed the bus.

05:35.568 --> 05:36.905
Oh, well, that's
all right, Meg.

05:36.973 --> 05:38.177
I can drive you to school.

05:38.245 --> 05:39.834
That'd be great. Thanks.

05:43.884 --> 05:46.276
So, uh... how are
your academics going?

05:46.361 --> 05:48.150
Good. Real good.

05:48.234 --> 05:50.041
That Puerto Rican street
gang give you any trouble

05:50.108 --> 05:51.614
on your way home from school?

05:51.664 --> 05:53.923
What Puerto Rican street gang?
You're welcome.

05:53.974 --> 05:55.429
Oh, hang on,
there's a red light.

05:55.480 --> 05:56.985
Got to hit the brakes.

05:57.069 --> 05:59.662
(exhaling)

05:59.730 --> 06:01.235
So, um...

06:01.303 --> 06:04.180
I hear you teenage girls are
pretty hot on that, uh...

06:04.248 --> 06:05.753
Nic Cage.

06:05.822 --> 06:08.966
Uh, no, not really.

06:09.034 --> 06:11.911
Okay.

06:11.978 --> 06:14.486
Hey, can you tell me
what Lady Gaga is?

06:14.554 --> 06:19.089
Is that a band, or a
soda, or a store, or...

06:19.157 --> 06:21.733
one of those terms
like "donkey punch"?

06:21.801 --> 06:22.703
No.

06:22.771 --> 06:24.343
Is it a douche?

06:26.319 --> 06:28.392
Is Lady Gaga a douche?

06:28.460 --> 06:30.233
I don't think so.

06:30.301 --> 06:31.907
Well, whatever it
is, I like it.

06:31.975 --> 06:33.797
Ah, green light.

06:33.865 --> 06:36.173
(blowing nose)

06:36.258 --> 06:38.934
Is... is it hard
being a paraplegic?

06:38.985 --> 06:40.692
Well, it's no picnic.

06:40.776 --> 06:43.703
Unless your version of a picnic
is being the basket.

06:43.787 --> 06:45.795
Well, you seem like you have
a good attitude about it.

06:45.846 --> 06:48.773
Yeah, you know, it's like we
handicapped people say:

06:48.840 --> 06:51.819
"When life ruins your legs,
you just gotta make legonade."

06:51.870 --> 06:54.194
I can sort of relate to that.

06:54.245 --> 06:56.369
You know, sometimes
it's really hard being me,

06:56.421 --> 06:58.478
and I guess I just
make Megonade.

06:58.545 --> 06:59.883
That sounds disgusting.

06:59.934 --> 07:01.105
All right, we're here.

07:02.278 --> 07:04.803
This is my school.

07:04.871 --> 07:07.264
Yeah, isn't that where
you wanted to go?

07:07.331 --> 07:08.969
Well, y-yeah, but...

07:09.037 --> 07:11.279
most times people just
drop me off a block away

07:11.346 --> 07:13.119
so they don't have
to be seen with me.

07:13.187 --> 07:14.291
Aw, that's gay.

07:14.358 --> 07:15.662
I don't mind being
seen with you.

07:15.746 --> 07:16.650
You don't?

07:16.718 --> 07:17.855
Of course not.

07:17.922 --> 07:19.796
Wow.

07:19.863 --> 07:22.088
Well, I-I better go,
I don't want to be tardy.

07:22.157 --> 07:24.397
Ah, that's not going to happen
from missing one class.

07:24.465 --> 07:25.935
People are born that way.

07:26.005 --> 07:27.293
Now run along,
or you'll be late.

07:31.577 --> 07:33.952
Hey, who's that,
your boyfriend?

07:34.019 --> 07:35.741
(cackling)

07:35.809 --> 07:37.583
Yeah.

07:37.668 --> 07:40.227
Yeah, that's my boyfriend.

07:46.053 --> 07:47.812
Meg, you're here early.

07:47.889 --> 07:49.694
Oh yeah, I just
wanted to make sure

07:49.762 --> 07:52.555
you got a nice hot breakfast
before you head off to work.

07:52.624 --> 07:54.898
Oh. Well, thanks.

07:54.966 --> 07:56.136
What's with the getup?

07:56.203 --> 07:57.342
Oh, nothing.

07:57.410 --> 07:59.750
I just wanted
to look sexy for Susie.

07:59.818 --> 08:01.909
How are your eggs, Joe?

08:01.977 --> 08:04.820
<i>MEG: If he doesn't say anything
about me calling him "Joe,"</i>

08:04.888 --> 08:06.829
<i>that means we're truly in love.</i>

08:06.897 --> 08:08.685
<i>JOE:
She just called me "Joe."</i>

08:08.754 --> 08:09.907
<i>That's kind of weird.</i>

08:09.975 --> 08:11.446
<i>But I'll just let it slide.</i>

08:11.514 --> 08:12.987
<i>She's got nothing going on.</i>

08:13.055 --> 08:15.062
<i>Besides, what harm could it do?</i>

08:15.113 --> 08:16.902
They're delicious,
Meg. Thanks.

08:16.970 --> 08:19.010
You're welcome, Joe.

08:19.078 --> 08:21.351
<i>JOE: Ah, (bleep), I should have
said something.</i>

08:21.420 --> 08:22.993
<i>MEG:
He let me say it twice now.</i>

08:23.061 --> 08:24.733
<i>It's like we're married.</i>

08:24.800 --> 08:26.907
<i>PATRICK STEWART:
This is Patrick Stewart.</i>

08:26.975 --> 08:29.283
<i>How are you liking
the program so far?</i>

08:45.382 --> 08:48.427
Aah! Oh, geez, you scared me.

08:48.495 --> 08:50.569
What happened
to your clothes?

08:50.636 --> 08:51.722
Hey, what are you doing?

08:55.020 --> 08:56.893
(screaming)

08:56.944 --> 08:58.701
(gagging)

09:04.023 --> 09:06.481
(labored breathing)

09:06.566 --> 09:07.618
Brian, have you seen...?

09:07.687 --> 09:09.277
Whoa, what the hell
happened to you?

09:09.328 --> 09:12.654
Easy, easy, man, easy.
(whimpering)

09:12.706 --> 09:15.400
(gasps)

09:15.467 --> 09:17.105
What the hell is
your problem?!

09:17.174 --> 09:18.579
Me? What did I do?

09:18.647 --> 09:20.386
You're the one going all
Michael Hutchence over here.

09:20.454 --> 09:22.277
You just stay away
from me, you psychopath.

09:22.344 --> 09:23.716
Hey, ow.

09:23.784 --> 09:25.506
Look, I don't know
what's going on here,

09:25.574 --> 09:27.447
but don't be throwing things,
because that's just not safe.

09:30.159 --> 09:31.915
(gasps)
What?

09:31.983 --> 09:34.174
Oh... my... God.

09:34.242 --> 09:37.085
Good Lord!

09:37.154 --> 09:39.629
I... am a genius.

09:39.698 --> 09:41.670
What... what is it?

09:41.738 --> 09:42.841
Don't you see, Brian?

09:42.909 --> 09:44.415
My machine did work.

09:44.483 --> 09:46.690
It created an evil clone
of me.

09:46.758 --> 09:48.062
That's why I didn't
feel more evil--

09:48.129 --> 09:49.669
all the evil energy
went into him.

09:49.737 --> 09:51.727
Well, kill it.
It almost choked me to death.

09:51.795 --> 09:53.333
I shall do
no such thing, Brian.

09:53.401 --> 09:54.839
It must be studied.

09:54.908 --> 09:57.349
If I can decode the genetic
puzzle of this being,

09:57.418 --> 09:59.257
perhaps I can determine
how to apply it

09:59.325 --> 10:00.779
to my own neurological makeup.

10:00.846 --> 10:02.587
Evil Stewie, come with me.

10:02.653 --> 10:04.712
We're going to run
a few tests on...

10:04.780 --> 10:06.167
(bone crunches)
(yelling)

10:06.235 --> 10:08.593
(grunting)

10:11.389 --> 10:12.359
(gasps)

10:15.371 --> 10:16.909
(whimpering)

10:16.961 --> 10:18.181
(yelling)

10:18.248 --> 10:20.173
(screaming)

10:22.132 --> 10:24.138
(grunting)

10:24.207 --> 10:25.610
(coughs)
(Brian screaming)

10:28.957 --> 10:30.714
(screaming continues)

10:35.452 --> 10:37.993
(tires squealing)

10:38.045 --> 10:40.052
Oh, my God, a baby!

10:40.136 --> 10:41.239
Are you okay?!

10:46.410 --> 10:48.250
(tires squealing)

10:51.933 --> 10:53.237
Hi, honey.

10:53.305 --> 10:54.307
What?

10:54.375 --> 10:55.379
What'd you say?

10:55.447 --> 10:56.951
I just said hi.

10:57.020 --> 11:00.064
Is that, uh-- is that
Bonnie's dress?

11:00.132 --> 11:01.937
Oh, yeah.
Susie spit up on me,

11:02.005 --> 11:04.447
and I didn't want
to go all the way home,

11:04.515 --> 11:05.620
so I just threw
this on.

11:05.688 --> 11:06.824
I hope that's okay.

11:06.892 --> 11:09.232
Yeah, it's fine,
I guess.

11:09.300 --> 11:11.676
Oh, here's that
juice box you asked for.

11:11.744 --> 11:13.400
Oh, thanks, Meg.

11:13.468 --> 11:14.972
Oh...
What's wrong?

11:15.039 --> 11:16.277
Oh, nothing.

11:16.346 --> 11:19.054
It's just that I like
to put the straw in myself.

11:19.122 --> 11:22.034
Oh, I-I'm sorry. Here.

11:22.102 --> 11:24.225
Yeah.
It's not the same now.

11:24.310 --> 11:26.685
I'll, uh, I'll just get
another one.

11:26.753 --> 11:27.890
(phone rings)

11:27.958 --> 11:28.960
I'll get it!

11:29.028 --> 11:30.652
Hello.

11:30.720 --> 11:32.056
Oh, hi, Meg, it's Bonnie.

11:32.124 --> 11:33.997
How is everything going there?

11:34.065 --> 11:35.035
Oh, great.

11:35.103 --> 11:36.107
Has Joe died?

11:36.175 --> 11:37.546
What? No.

11:37.613 --> 11:39.083
That's good.

11:39.152 --> 11:41.661
I was just calling to tell him
my father is recovering well

11:41.729 --> 11:43.703
and the doctors say
he'll be fine.

11:43.771 --> 11:45.744
That's great. I'll tell him.

11:45.813 --> 11:48.355
I'll be flying back
first thing in the morning.

11:48.423 --> 11:50.027
That's great, too.

11:50.095 --> 11:53.341
Okay, bye, Bonnie.
See ya tomorrow.

11:53.409 --> 11:54.361
Bye.

11:54.429 --> 11:55.633
Who was that?

11:55.684 --> 11:57.390
Oh, uh, prank call.

11:57.458 --> 11:59.866
Oh, yeah, I, uh, get
a lot of those.

11:59.934 --> 12:02.242
I can never figure
out who it is.

12:02.311 --> 12:03.983
Who is this?

12:04.051 --> 12:06.394
PETER: Wheely-wheely stupid head,
but you wish that you were dead.

12:06.461 --> 12:08.033
Listen, I don't know who
this is,

12:08.100 --> 12:10.441
but you better cut it out!
I'm a cop, you know!

12:10.510 --> 12:12.985
Oh, what, are you gonna report
me on your can't walkie-talkie?

12:13.054 --> 12:14.524
I'm gonna hang up now.

12:14.591 --> 12:15.930
No, no, no, wait, wait, wait!

12:15.998 --> 12:17.670
I got three more of these
I wrote on a napkin.

12:17.738 --> 12:19.812
(sighs) All right, three more.

12:25.870 --> 12:27.910
(snoring)

12:57.061 --> 12:58.515
(jet engines roar)

13:13.124 --> 13:15.381
(beeping)

13:15.449 --> 13:17.908
Ma'am, is this your bag?

13:17.976 --> 13:20.418
I don't know how that cocaine
got in there.

13:20.485 --> 13:22.561
Ma'am, this bag contains
a concealed weapon.

13:22.629 --> 13:24.703
I'm gonna have to place you
under arrest.

13:24.770 --> 13:27.379
Oh, my goodness,
how did that get in there?

13:27.464 --> 13:29.387
You're gonna have
to come with us, ma'am.

13:29.472 --> 13:30.742
(handcuffs click)
What happened to the coke?

13:30.810 --> 13:32.316
There's no coke
in here.

13:32.383 --> 13:34.390
Oh, (bleep),
Ricardo's gonna kill me.

13:42.580 --> 13:43.785
This is nice, Joe.

13:43.844 --> 13:47.775
A night out, a good dinner.
Thank you so much.

13:47.844 --> 13:49.247
Well, I wanted
to do something special.

13:49.315 --> 13:50.519
Show you how much
I appreciate

13:50.587 --> 13:52.092
all the hard work
you've been doing.

13:52.159 --> 13:53.397
Oh, it's been my pleasure.

13:53.465 --> 13:54.837
So, listen,
there's something

13:54.888 --> 13:56.827
I wanted to talk
to you about.

13:56.895 --> 13:58.033
What's that?

13:58.101 --> 14:00.643
Do you ever think
about having another baby?

14:00.711 --> 14:02.550
I don't know.

14:02.617 --> 14:03.788
I guess I'm open
to it.

14:03.856 --> 14:05.663
Really? Oh, that's great!

14:05.731 --> 14:07.135
So, I'll get off the pill...

14:07.203 --> 14:08.441
What do you mean?

14:08.509 --> 14:10.616
Nothing. Nothing. Forget it.

14:10.684 --> 14:13.091
I-I think I'm just
a little scattered tonight.

14:13.160 --> 14:14.966
I'm probably just PMS-ing

14:15.034 --> 14:16.303
Oh, grody.

14:16.372 --> 14:18.178
Hey, this is supposed
to be a fun night.

14:18.247 --> 14:19.283
What's wrong
with you?

14:19.351 --> 14:21.558
You know, I could ask
the same of you.

14:21.626 --> 14:24.069
We haven't made love
in two weeks.

14:24.136 --> 14:25.826
We haven't made
love ever!

14:25.877 --> 14:27.097
(crying)

14:27.165 --> 14:30.042
Oh, great!
Now you've upset the baby!

14:32.954 --> 14:36.735
(gasping) Oh, God! Oh!

14:36.803 --> 14:40.735
<i>PATRICK STEWART: This feels right, but
it tastes like a dirty penny.</i>

14:43.949 --> 14:45.236
This is ridiculous.

14:45.287 --> 14:46.373
Evil Stewie could
be anywhere.

14:46.425 --> 14:48.097
You know, this really
is all your fault.

14:48.181 --> 14:50.055
If you hadn't told me
I was going soft

14:50.106 --> 14:51.360
I wouldn't have
created Evil Stewie,

14:51.427 --> 14:52.731
he wouldn't have escaped

14:52.783 --> 14:54.874
and we wouldn't be trying
to track down a murderer.

14:54.941 --> 14:57.433
For all we know he could be
killing someone else right now.

14:57.502 --> 14:58.437
(normal pitched):
Oh, no.

14:58.506 --> 14:59.442
(deep voice):
Oh, no.

14:59.510 --> 15:00.345
(high-pitched):
Oh, no!

15:00.430 --> 15:01.668
Oh, yeah!

15:01.736 --> 15:02.588
(groaning)

15:09.350 --> 15:11.991
Listen, guys, I got
something to tell you.

15:12.058 --> 15:14.301
And I don't really know
how to break it to you,

15:14.370 --> 15:16.810
so I'm just going to come
right out and say it.

15:16.879 --> 15:18.349
Meg has a crush on me.

15:18.418 --> 15:22.465
(both laughing)

15:22.533 --> 15:25.277
Oh, my God!
Get over yourself!

15:25.345 --> 15:27.954
Well, look, all I'm saying is,

15:28.022 --> 15:30.732
I remember when Brian had
a similar difficulty with Meg.

15:30.801 --> 15:34.012
Maybe she's prone to quick
and severe infatuation.

15:34.080 --> 15:35.685
Yeah, with a dog,
not a cripple.

15:35.753 --> 15:37.525
Hey, easy there.

15:37.593 --> 15:39.299
All right,
look, maybe I'm wrong.

15:39.368 --> 15:41.977
Maybe I misread a few
of Meg's signals.

15:42.045 --> 15:44.487
Sorry I bothered you.

15:46.278 --> 15:49.623
Excuse me, Lois, I have
to go make a phone call.

15:49.691 --> 15:51.063
(phone dialing)

15:51.131 --> 15:52.435
Hey, wheely stupid head,

15:52.502 --> 15:54.141
I heard you think
Meg likes you.

15:54.209 --> 15:55.379
JOE:
Who is this?!

15:55.447 --> 15:57.254
How are you getting
this information?!

15:58.459 --> 15:59.897
(sniffs)

15:59.966 --> 16:02.274
Oh, my God, Joe was here.

16:02.342 --> 16:03.445
Yeah, he just left.

16:03.513 --> 16:06.323
I know. I can feel him.

16:06.391 --> 16:08.079
I can smell him.

16:08.164 --> 16:09.904
Mm, I can taste him.

16:09.971 --> 16:12.314
Okay, I get the smell part.

16:12.382 --> 16:14.756
But, Meg, I think we
have to have a talk.

16:14.824 --> 16:16.831
Sweetheart, you don't--

16:16.899 --> 16:18.939
you don't have a crush
on Joe, do you?

16:19.007 --> 16:21.784
Um... I don't know.

16:21.852 --> 16:24.964
Oh, my God, you do have
a crush on him.

16:25.031 --> 16:27.155
What, Mom?
Why shouldn't I like him?

16:27.224 --> 16:29.280
When I'm with him,
he makes me happy.

16:29.348 --> 16:31.054
And he needs me.

16:31.122 --> 16:33.429
Oh, Meg,
you're fooling yourself.

16:33.497 --> 16:35.973
It's classic
Florence Nightingale Syndrome.

16:36.041 --> 16:38.248
You're taking care of him
and you're feeling a closeness

16:38.317 --> 16:41.027
that you're misinterpreting
as a romantic connection.

16:41.094 --> 16:42.566
But think about it, Meg.

16:42.634 --> 16:44.105
You two have
nothing in common.

16:44.173 --> 16:46.315
You know, you're right, Mom.

16:46.382 --> 16:48.991
I hear you loud and clear.

17:00.823 --> 17:02.462
(thumping)
(screaming)

17:02.530 --> 17:06.041
(tires squealing)

17:06.109 --> 17:08.168
Meg, what the hell
did you do?!

17:08.236 --> 17:10.443
I made us the same, Joe.

17:10.511 --> 17:13.087
We're exactly alike, you and I.

17:13.156 --> 17:15.731
Now we can be together.

17:15.799 --> 17:17.538
My God, we have to get you
to the hospital.

17:22.542 --> 17:24.849
(siren wailing)
(tires squealing)

17:24.918 --> 17:27.193
No, but I mean after
soccer practice.

17:27.261 --> 17:29.033
You got anything
planned for then?

17:29.101 --> 17:30.355
(siren wailing)

17:30.406 --> 17:31.526
I mean, nothing,
nothing.

17:31.577 --> 17:33.133
Keep walking.
You don't know me.

17:40.027 --> 17:41.850
The doctor says
you're going to be fine.

17:41.917 --> 17:43.490
And your family's on the way.

17:43.559 --> 17:46.101
But that was a crazy
thing you did, Meg.

17:46.169 --> 17:47.305
I know.

17:47.374 --> 17:49.615
I'm... I'm so sorry.

17:49.682 --> 17:51.455
I just wanted us
to be closer.

17:51.523 --> 17:53.329
Look, Meg, I do
care for you,

17:53.398 --> 17:56.275
but I care for you like
I... I would a niece

17:56.342 --> 17:58.048
or a good friend's
daughter.

17:58.116 --> 18:00.725
(sighs)
I feel like such an idiot.

18:00.793 --> 18:03.469
Don't. I'm lucky
to have you as a neighbor,

18:03.538 --> 18:06.247
and even luckier
to have you as a friend.

18:06.315 --> 18:10.196
Thanks. I'm lucky
to have you as a friend, too.

18:10.264 --> 18:12.404
(sighs) When is
Bonnie coming home?

18:12.472 --> 18:14.413
I have to
apologize to her.

18:14.480 --> 18:16.420
Well, you can
apologize right now.

18:16.505 --> 18:17.676
Hi, Meg.

18:17.743 --> 18:20.118
Bonnie, I'm so sorry
I got you arrested.

18:20.186 --> 18:21.993
No, it's all right, Meg.

18:22.060 --> 18:26.242
Look, I was a teenage girl
with a crush at one time myself.

18:26.310 --> 18:29.289
I know sometimes
it makes you lose touch.

18:29.356 --> 18:30.626
Thanks for being
so understanding.

18:30.694 --> 18:33.037
I-I hope I didn't get you
into too much trouble.

18:33.105 --> 18:35.730
I mean, you're not gonna go
to jail or anything, are you?

18:35.798 --> 18:37.637
No, I'll be around.

18:37.704 --> 18:41.352
I need these voice-over checks to
support my gambling addiction.

18:46.825 --> 18:48.028
Evil Stewie?

18:48.096 --> 18:50.171
Wherever you are,
if you can hear me,

18:50.238 --> 18:52.112
I'm completely
defenseless right now.

18:56.379 --> 18:58.855
Okay, there you are.

18:58.923 --> 19:01.097
Well, this is a gift, Brian.

19:01.165 --> 19:03.942
Thank you for making it so easy.

19:04.026 --> 19:06.285
Hey, well, you know,
you're doing me a favor.

19:06.369 --> 19:09.012
I've had enough; I can't live with that
stupid family anymore.

19:09.080 --> 19:12.057
Do me a favor and end it
all for me, will ya?

19:12.125 --> 19:14.300
Delighted to
oblige, Brian.

19:18.248 --> 19:19.571
Aah!

19:27.285 --> 19:30.163
(blows landing loudly)

19:37.191 --> 19:39.349
(weapon blasting)

19:52.769 --> 19:54.960
(blows landing loudly)

20:29.597 --> 20:32.106
Oh, come on,
not this thing! Really?

20:32.175 --> 20:33.580
Brian, it's me, Stewie.

20:33.647 --> 20:35.655
<i>Shoot him!
No! Brian, you know me.</i>

20:35.723 --> 20:37.193
<i>Look at me.
Shoot him.</i>

20:37.262 --> 20:39.536
All right, there's
only one way to settle this.

20:39.604 --> 20:40.842
Look at your feet.

20:40.910 --> 20:42.281
Why? They're just feet.

20:42.349 --> 20:43.452
(giggling)

20:43.519 --> 20:44.991
Wh-What are they
doing down there?

20:45.058 --> 20:46.431
They're like leg hands!

20:49.025 --> 20:51.200
(sizzling)

20:52.990 --> 20:54.846
Nice job, man!

20:54.914 --> 20:56.119
Wow!

20:56.187 --> 20:57.625
That was really
brilliant.

20:57.692 --> 20:59.565
Thanks. Just glad
this nightmare is over.

20:59.633 --> 21:02.192
And I'm really glad I
didn't kill the wrong Stewie.

21:02.261 --> 21:03.431
Yeah, me, too.

21:03.498 --> 21:05.070
Hey, come on,
I'll take you home.

21:08.100 --> 21:11.262
(deep, echoing, evil laughter)

21:11.263 --> 22:12.263
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.ru